      "writtenOn": "2026-02-26T07:52:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IMPORTANT: For inverse transforms, use cos_bit\u003d12.\n\nNote: If I change cos_bit to 12 here, I also need to change the `input` array to cause signed integer overflow:\n\n```\n  int32_t input[4] \u003d { 300000, 0, 300000, 300000 };\n  int32_t output[4];\n\n  av1_iadst4(input, output, 12, range_bit);\n```\n\nSee libaom source code:\n\n```\n// Values in both av1_inv_cos_bit_col and av1_inv_cos_bit_row are always 12\n// for each valid row and col combination\n#define INV_COS_BIT 12\n```\n\nand the AV1 spec, section 7.13.2.6. Inverse ADST4 process:\n\n```\nT[ 0 ] \u003d Round2( x[ 0 ], 12 )\nT[ 1 ] \u003d Round2( x[ 1 ], 12 )\nT[ 2 ] \u003d Round2( x[ 2 ], 12 )\nT[ 3 ] \u003d Round2( x[ 3 ], 12 )\n```",
      "revId": "ed3353fc7d0c3ef7c18f0a4bf2a386a9c1874bce",
